Handle LIBINPUT_SWITCH_KEYPAD_SLIDE in handle_switch_toggle.

WHY: wlroots 0.19.1 builds with -Werror and -Wswitch, and libinput 1.31.3
defines a switch type that wlroots 0.19.1 predates. The build failed at
object 205 of 342:

    ../backend/libinput/switch.c:32:9: error: enumeration value
        'LIBINPUT_SWITCH_KEYPAD_SLIDE' not handled in switch [-Werror=switch]
    cc1: all warnings being treated as errors

THIS IS VERSION SKEW BETWEEN TWO PINS, NOT A BUG IN EITHER. `switch` over an
enum with no `default:` is deliberate style in wlroots -- it is what makes
-Wswitch tell you when upstream libinput grows a case -- and libinput adding
one is ordinary. The two pins were chosen independently and this is where
they meet.

WHY THIS PATCH RATHER THAN -Dwerror=false. Turning off -Werror would silence
every warning in 342 objects to fix one, and would hide exactly the class of
message that produced this one. wlroots' own choice not to write `default:`
is the mechanism working; the answer is to add the case, not to disable the
check that found it.

WHY NOT MAP IT TO A wlr_switch_type. wlroots has WLR_SWITCH_TYPE_LID and
WLR_SWITCH_TYPE_TABLET_MODE and nothing else -- adding a third is a public
API change to a pinned library, which is a much larger claim than this patch
should make. The event is ignored instead, which is what wlroots 0.19.1
already does with it today: with no case and no default, the switch falls
through and `wlr_event.switch_type` keeps its zero-initialised value. This
makes that behaviour EXPLICIT and silent rather than implicit and fatal.

WHAT THAT COSTS, STATED: a keypad-slide switch event is delivered to the
compositor as switch_type 0, which is WLR_SWITCH_TYPE_LID. That is wrong, and
it is what the unpatched code would do if -Werror were merely disabled. The
`return` avoids it -- the event is dropped rather than mislabelled, which is
the honest reading of "wlroots 0.19.1 does not know what this is".

Hardware affected: none in this set. No keypad-slide device exists under
qemu, and the boot probe reports two evdev nodes, both virtio.

--- a/backend/libinput/switch.c
+++ b/backend/libinput/switch.c
@@ -36,6 +36,11 @@
 	case LIBINPUT_SWITCH_TABLET_MODE:
 		wlr_event.switch_type = WLR_SWITCH_TYPE_TABLET_MODE;
 		break;
+	case LIBINPUT_SWITCH_KEYPAD_SLIDE:
+		/* libinput 1.31 added this; wlroots 0.19 has no wlr_switch_type
+		 * for it. Drop the event rather than deliver it as switch_type 0,
+		 * which is WLR_SWITCH_TYPE_LID. */
+		return;
 	}
 	switch (libinput_event_switch_get_switch_state(sevent)) {
 	case LIBINPUT_SWITCH_STATE_OFF:
